.TH SWAYLOCK-WARPMAN 1 "2026" "warpman" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swaylock-warpman \- screen locker for sway with the warpman drift animation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaylock-warpman
[\fIswaylock options\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIdrift options\fR]
.br
.B swaylock-warpman \-\-preview
[\fIdrift options\fR]
.br
.B swaylock-warpman \-\-background
[\fIdrift options\fR]
.br
.B swaylock-warpman \-\-help\-swaylock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swaylock-warpman
is swaylock-plugin (built in) with the warpman drift animation as its background:
a thin tinted grid on black, bent by slowly wandering lenses, rendered with OpenGL on
every monitor at its native resolution.
.PP
Without a mode option it locks the screen. \fB\-f\fR (daemonize) and \fB\-c 000000\fR
are passed to swaylock-plugin unless \fB\-\-no\-daemonize\fR is given, and the
background command is set to \fBswaylock-warpman \-\-background\fR plus any drift
options after \fB\-\-\fR. All other options are swaylock-plugin's
(\fB\-\-help\-swaylock\fR lists them); its config file is ~/.config/swaylock/config.
.PP
\fB\-\-preview\fR shows the animation above the windows of the running compositor
for 10 seconds (clicks pass through). \fB\-\-background\fR is what the locker runs.
.PP
Authentication uses the PAM service \fBswaylock-warpman\fR (/etc/pam.d/swaylock-warpman).
.SH DRIFT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Frame rate (default 24).
.TP
.BI \-\-new\-scene\-every " SEC"
Switch to a new random scene every SEC seconds; 0 = never (default 300).
.TP
.BI \-\-hue " DEG" "\fR|\fPrandom"
Tint hue (default 120, green).
.TP
.BI \-\-saturation " S" "\fR|\fPrandom"
Tint saturation 0\-1 (default 0.5).
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Seed of the first scene (the same seed gives the same scene as the Python warpman).
.TP
.BI \-\-lenses " N"
Number of lenses; 0 = random 1\-3.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " PX"
Lens speed in px/s at 1280 wide (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-rainbow " MODE"
off, wave, ripple or cycle.
.TP
.BI \-\-rainbow\-speed " HZ"
Spectrum cycles per second (default 0.1).
.TP
.BR \-\-status " / " \-\-no\-status
CPU and battery text in the bottom-right corner (default on).
.TP
.BR \-\-still\-on\-battery " / " \-\-animate\-on\-battery
Pause the animation on battery power (default: pause).
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " SEC"
Exit after SEC seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-layer background\fR|\fBoverlay
Layer-shell layer of the client.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
DRIFT_FPS, DRIFT_SCENE_SECONDS, DRIFT_HUE, DRIFT_SATURATION, DRIFT_STATUS (0 hides the
text), DRIFT_ANIMATE_ON_BATTERY (1 keeps animating), DRIFT_SEED, DRIFT_LENSES,
DRIFT_SPEED, DRIFT_RAINBOW and DRIFT_RAINBOW_SPEED set the defaults of the options
above.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/warpman-lock.log
Background log, started afresh on each lock.
.SH EXAMPLE
In the sway config:
.PP
.nf
set $lock swaylock-warpman
exec swayidle \-w timeout 300 $lock before\-sleep $lock
bindsym $mod+BackSpace exec $lock
bindsym \-\-locked $mod+Ctrl+BackSpace exec 'pkill \-x swaylock-warpman; $lock'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swayidle (1),
.BR i3lock-warpman (1)
